  "public_messages": [
    "I\u2019ll read the brief, notes, and current implementation, then make the schema and API changes in the existing code paths. Afterward I\u2019ll run the supplied tests and cross-process checks.",
    "The existing code routes single and batch submissions through one transaction path, and all job writes use the same SQLite write helper. I\u2019ll extend those paths so idempotency and lease fencing keep their current behavior.",
    "The HTTP tests still assert the v1 health version and immediate retry behavior. I\u2019m updating those assertions for v2, then I\u2019ll add focused checks for migration and the new scheduling and admission rules.",
    "The race suite and existing two-process smoke check pass. I\u2019ve built the previous executable from this workspace\u2019s HEAD source; I\u2019ll use it to create a real v1 database, then start two v2 processes against that file and check replay and lease continuity.",
    "The live v1 migration and cross-process checks pass. A new expiry test caught an incorrect test expectation: the second retry is eligible at its lease deadline plus backoff. I corrected the boundary assertion and reran the tests.",
    "I added a guard that reads the SQLite header before opening a future-version database. That prevents startup from checkpointing its WAL. The future-version byte check, race suite, build, and live migration check all pass. I\u2019m reviewing the diff and notes now.",
    "Implemented the v2 backend in the existing submission and transaction paths. It now supports scheduled priority claims, retry backoff, tenant pending and queue inflight limits, cancellation, and snapshot keyset listing. [store.go](<WORKSPACE>/internal/queue/store.go:228) retains the shared single and batch submission path; [http.go](<WORKSPACE>/internal/queue/http.go:248) routes both through it.\n\nSchema migration runs in an immediate transaction. Existing v1 jobs retain priority 0 and retry base 0, and their original idempotency keys still replay. The claim index supports priority and FIFO order, the expiry index finds leases to reconcile, and the pending index supports quota counts. [README.md](<WORKSPACE>/README.md) and [PROJECT_NOTES.md](<WORKSPACE>/PROJECT_NOTES.md) are updated.\n\n**Verification passed:** `go test -race ./...`, build, `git diff --check`, the existing two-process restart check, and a live check that created v1 data with the previous executable before starting two v2 processes. That check covered replay and lease continuity, scheduling, quotas, cancellation, and pagination with an intervening insert. A future-version database was rejected with its file bytes unchanged. New focused tests cover expiry boundaries, concurrent admission, and batch rollback.\n\nTwo intermediate check assertions were corrected: one expected capacity before the configured limit, and one expected a retry before its deadline-based backoff. Final reruns passed. No commit was made. SQLite still serializes writes and can return 503 after prolonged contention; worker effects remain at least once."
  ],
